## 2. Grant — one machine, free, any purpose

The licensor grants you a **worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive,
non-transferable and non-sublicensable** licence to:

1. **install and run** the Software;
2. **make copies** of the Software as reasonably necessary to install, run and
   back it up on machines you control;
3. **modify your own copy** of the Software for your own use, including to fix
   it or adapt it to your hardware;

— on **up to one (1) serving machine managed together** (§1.3), together with
**any number of control-plane machines**, for **any purpose whatsoever,
including commercial production use inside a for-profit organisation**.

**No licence file is required in this mode.** No registration, no activation,
no account, no payment details, no phone-home. The Software contains no
telemetry and this licence does not introduce any. You do not have to tell us
you are using it.

A company running its production inference on one serving machine is fully
licensed and owes nothing. That is intended, not an oversight.

---

## 3. Two or more serving machines

Operating **two or more serving machines managed together** (§1.3) requires a
**commercial licence** or a valid **trial licence**.

This is also where the Software itself asks for a licence file. The boundary in
this section and the boundary the Software enforces are deliberately identical,
so there is no state in which you are running normally but are nonetheless in
breach. **If it runs, you are licensed.**

For the avoidance of doubt, the following require a commercial licence
**regardless of machine count, including on a single machine**:

- using the Software to deliver a product or service to third parties;
- installing or operating the Software for a customer as an integrator,
  consultancy or managed service provider;
- redistribution, resale, hosting-as-a-service, white-labelling, rebranding,
  OEM distribution, or sub-licensing (see also §8).

---

## 4. Trial licence — automatic, self-service, free

Trial licences are **issued automatically on request**. There is no human in
the loop, no sales conversation, no approval step, and **no payment details are
required or requested**.

- **What it unlocks:** unlimited serving machines, for **30 days**.
- **What it is for:** evaluating the Software, including multi-machine and
  stacked deployment, before deciding whether to buy.

### 4.1 Cooldown between trials

**After a trial expires, a new trial licence is issued 7 days later, not
sooner.** That 7-day cooldown is a term of this licence, stated here so you
know the rule in advance rather than meeting it as a refusal.

During the cooldown:

- your machine limit returns to **one** (§2), for **new operations only**;
- **nothing you are running is switched off** — §10 applies in full, and every
  model already deployed keeps running on every machine, with `start`, `stop`,
  `restart`, `logs`, `ps`, `doctor` and `status` available on all of them,
  including automatic start at boot;
- your right to run on one machine, and every right in §9, is unaffected.

Longer evaluations and extensions are available — ask, and we will arrange one
rather than making you wait out a cooldown. The cooldown exists to keep the
trial self-service, not to make evaluation difficult.

### 4.2 Expiry

When a trial expires you return to the free one-machine tier **for new
operations only**, on exactly the terms in §4.1 above.

A machine that reboots at 3am after a trial lapsed comes back up. This licence
is never used as a kill switch, and §10 states that as a binding term rather
than a promise.

---

## 5. What is always free, at every tier

The following are never gated, never removed, and never reserved to a paid
tier, regardless of your machine count, your subscription status, or whether
you hold any licence file at all:

quality gates · `doctor` · `repair` · `validate` · `preflight` · secret
redaction · allowlists · approval prompts before risky operations · and any
other feature whose purpose is to stop a deployment from harming you or your
data.

Limits in this licence are limits of **scale**, never of **safety**.

---

## 6. The subscription is available at every tier, including free

The recipe catalog and support subscription described in `COMMERCIAL.md` is
**purchasable by anyone, including users on the free one-machine tier**. It
does not require a commercial licence and does not require you to run more than
one machine.

**Free is a machine count, not a feature ceiling.** A one-machine company that
wants the hardware-proven recipe catalog and a support channel can buy exactly
that, and nothing else.

A subscription does not raise your machine limit, and lapsing one does not
lower it. The two are independent.

---

## 7. Reserved rights

All commercial use beyond §2, §4 and §6 is reserved to the licensor and is
available only under a commercial licence. To obtain one, see `COMMERCIAL.md`
and §16.

---

## 8. No sharing, no forking, no sublicensing

This section is unchanged in substance from the NOTICE in force today, and it
applies at **every** tier, paid tiers included.

You may **not**:

- distribute, publish, mirror, host, or otherwise make the Software available
  to anyone else, in source or built form;
- **fork** the repository — with or without modification, with or without the
  original name;
- publish or share your modifications to the Software;
- sublicense the Software or purport to grant anyone else any right in it;
- remove, alter or obscure this licence, the `NOTICE` file, copyright notices,
  attribution, or provenance headers.

Modifications you make under §2.3 are for **your own use on machines you
control**. They stay there.

**The source is published so that it can be read and audited. Reading it,
cloning it, or receiving a copy of it grants you nothing beyond the rights in
§2.**

*(Partner and OEM agreements may grant sub-licensing rights. Those rights come
from that signed agreement, not from this file.)*

---

## 9. Bundles you generate are yours

**Deployment bundles generated by the Software (controller scripts,
`README.md`, `MODEL_PROFILE.yaml`, `SPECIAL_FILES.md` and checksum manifests)
belong to the person who generated them and may be used, modified and
redistributed freely.**

This does not depend on your tier. It does not depend on having a licence file
or a subscription. It is not revoked when this licence terminates, when a trial
expires, during a cooldown, or when a commercial agreement ends. It applies to
bundles generated for commercial production exactly as it applies to bundles
generated at home. Nothing in §3, §4, §7, §8 or §11 restricts what you do with
a bundle you generated.

The generator that produces bundles is not covered by this section. **Bundles
are yours to run and to keep. The generator that produces them is not.**

If a bundle carries a `licensed_to`, `license_id` or `attestation` stamp, that
stamp records where the bundle came from. It is a provenance mark, not a
restriction on the bundle, and removing it does not make the bundle more yours
than it already is.

---

## 10. Nothing running is ever switched off

The Software will not stop, kill, disable or degrade a model that is already
deployed, on account of licence status, at any tier, ever.

Expiry, lapse, cooldown, downgrade and termination affect **new** operations
only — deploying, pushing and cloning beyond the free limit. Inspection and
lifecycle control of existing deployments (`start`, `stop`, `restart`, `logs`,
`ps`, `doctor`, `status`), including automatic start at boot, remain available.

This is a term of this licence, not a product promise, and it survives
termination.

---

## 11. Term and termination

**11.1 The free one-machine tier is a standing grant.** It takes effect when
you first obtain a copy of the Software and continues for as long as you comply
with this licence. It is **not** revocable at the licensor's discretion and
requires nothing from you to keep.

**11.2 Termination for breach.** If you breach this licence, your rights under
§2 terminate. If the breach can be cured and you cure it within **30 days** of
becoming aware of it, and it is your first breach, your rights are reinstated
automatically.

**11.3 Future versions.** The licensor may licence future versions of the
Software on different terms. Doing so does not alter the terms applying to any
version already published — see §12.

**11.4 Trial, subscription and commercial licences** run for their stated terms
and are governed additionally by their own terms. A trial that lapses is not a
breach; it simply returns you to §2. A subscription that lapses is not a breach
and does not change your machine limit.

**11.5 Survival.** Sections 9, 10, 12, 13, 14, 15 and 16 survive termination.

---

## 12. Which versions this covers

**This licence applies to every version of the Software, including versions
published or obtained before this licence was published.**

If you cloned the repository under its earlier terms — which granted no right
to use the Software at all — this licence applies to that copy too, and you
are covered by it. Nobody needs to re-download anything to become licensed,
and there is no version of LMDS that anyone is running unlicensed.

